# Date arithmetic with large offsets

Adding days or months and subtracting dates take time independent of the size
of the offset (the offsets stay within 32-bit integers, for the Java runtime).

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope LargeOffsets:
  output far_days content date
  output far_months content date
  output back content duration
  output year_before content date
  output two_years_before content date

scope LargeOffsets:
  definition far_days equals |2000-01-01| + 2000000000 day
  definition far_months equals |2000-01-01| + 2000000000 month
  definition back equals far_days - |2000-01-01|
  definition year_before equals |2000-01-15| - 12 month
  definition two_years_before equals |2000-01-15| - 24 month
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope LargeOffsets
┌─[RESULT]─ LargeOffsets ─
│ far_days = |5477814-01-06|
│ far_months = |166668666-09-01|
│ back = [2000000000 days]
│ year_before = |1999-01-15|
│ two_years_before = |1998-01-15|
└─
```
